# Spec-Driven Development

Apply when working in this repo's `docs/` tree or `AGENTS.md`. Read `docs/.sdd.yaml` first.

**The specification — not the code, not the prompt — is the source of truth.** The plugin owns the spec/document layer and the delivery pipeline that runs on it — workers, review, triage, close-out. A general engineering plugin is optional, and only at the exploration end.

**SDD commands:** `/sdd-scaffold` · `/sdd-specify` · `/sdd-deliver` (`--close-out`) · `/sdd-review` · `/sdd-triage` · `/sdd-trace` (`--audit`). For the full flow, use the `spec-driven-development` skill or — in a scaffolded repo — [docs/ai-workflow.md](docs/ai-workflow.md).

**Load-bearing rules:** one canonical home per requirement (index links, spec owns the prose); identifiers immutable once published; don't mix document kinds; don't settle open questions silently (STRAND, ADR, or ask); look domain facts up in the named ground-truth source. No code-first without a `REQ`/spec — `/sdd-specify` first. One home per fact in process prose too — commit body / PR body / changelog / review threads cite identifiers rather than restating. Findings live in `.sdd/findings/<branch>.md` (git-ignored); critical and important are resolved before merge, suggestions never block; `sdd-pr status` says what is open. Two profiles: formal (requirements, RFC-2119 specs, the traceability map) and informative (a knowledge base plus one binding constitution). Plans are not the plugin's business. Every `docs/` document declares its kind; generated blocks are written by `sdd-check generate`; the gate is `spec-check`.
